var e=`It has just come to me that I did not press the lid down properly on the tub with my leftover lasagne in it. The risk of a sauce explosion is too high.(The Fire Safety Officer has been on the phone. I have to count the sockets in the table football room as a matter of the utmost urgency.(I absolutely must find out how to switch our break room microwave from 600 to 800 watts. This is strictly one for the top.(Under the new health and safety regulations my desk is standing two centimetres too far to the left. I have to wait for the measuring service.(I have been asked at short notice to clean the windows in Room 104. The head of department's view is apparently milky.(The expired soya milk in the fridge has by now founded a works council of its own. I have been called in to mediate.(This morning I drank from the pot of decaffeinated filter coffee by mistake. My body is running on emergency power.(A pigeon has been staring at me through the window in judgement for ten minutes now. If I break eye contact at this point, I have lost.(The caretaker needs help deciphering a handwritten note on the paper skip. This could take a while.(My desk plant has come down with acute sunburn. I must administer first aid with the spray bottle immediately.(The canteen rissole is sitting extremely heavily. My digestive tract has convened an ad hoc meeting.(I can feel a slight scratching in my throat, which points to an allergic reaction to the new carpet cleaner. I need quarantine.(My feng shui consultant has forbidden me to take any far-reaching decisions, on account of unfavourable currents in the earth's magnetic field.(I need to step out into the corridor. Somebody called 'Hello?' and I want to make sure no intern has gone missing.(The blind is jammed at half mast. If I simply carry on working now, I shall end up with an asymmetrical sunburn on my nose.(I urgently need to calibrate my paper scissors. On A4 sheets they no longer cut at an exact ninety-degree angle.(The delivery service has rung, my Asian noodle salad keeps missing the front door. I have to talk the driver in.(The carpet crackled nastily as I walked across it. I am statically charged and may not look at anybody for the time being.(Somebody has written 'Please allways wash up' on the note in the kitchen. I must track down the culprit.(I have to go and check whether the clock in the big meeting room is still two minutes fast. One can never be too sure.(A colleague sneezed in the corridor and I did not say 'bless you' quickly enough. I have to find him and apologise properly.(The strip light above my desk is flickering in time to 'Stayin' Alive'. I urgently need to fetch the baton.(I have the distinct impression that my notepad has filled up. I must apply to Stores for fresh blank pages.(The coffee machine put out no residual water after rinsing today. I have to investigate where the water has got to.(I have a slight twinge in my left earlobe. According to the emergency medical advice on the internet I now need absolute silence.(My seat cushion has slipped and I do not dare tug it straight again in front of the whole office. I need a private room.(I urgently need to practise my signature on a scrap of paper. On the holiday request form today it looked somehow forged.(It has come back to me that this morning I left the iron... hold on, I do not iron. But I do need a moment to work through the shock.(I have been nominated as a neutral witness, to observe how often the water cooler gurgles when a cup is drawn.(I believe I have hung my jacket in the wrong cloakroom locker. It is setting off a deep spiritual dissonance in me.(My hole punch made a slightly muffled sound while punching today. It needs reassurance and, urgently, a clean.(My left eye twitches every single time I try to be productive. That is a clear warning to me from the universe.(The radiator under my desk has been gurgling all morning. I have been asked to talk to it kindly until the plumber turns up some time next week.(I feel the sudden, uncontrollable urge to sort every paperclip at my desk by size and angle of bend.(I have to establish at length why the toilet paper on the second floor has been hung the wrong way round again. A clear act of protest.(Somebody has used my favourite mug and not put it in the dishwasher. I need time to work through this betrayal.(The shredder smells faintly of burnt plastic. Somebody has to keep an eye on it, and as a hero of labour I am volunteering.(I have to verify whether the soap dispenser in the gents really does deliver exactly three squirts for one washing of the hands.(My left shoe is pressing suspiciously on my big toe. If I take a call now, my calf is guaranteed to seize up.(The pens in my desk tidy are no longer parallel to one another. This asymmetry inhibits all creative and administrative flow.`.split(`(`);export{e as excuses};